The purpose of this chapter is to promote harmonious relationships in the interaction between human beings and animals by:
(1) Protecting animals from improper use, abuse, neglect, exploitation, inhumane treatment and health hazards;
(2) Delineating the animal owner's or harborer's responsibility for the acts and behavior of such person's animal at all times;
(3) Providing security to residents from annoyance, intimidation, injury and health hazards by animals; and
(4) Encouraging responsible pet ownership.
(Code 1979, § 2-4002; Ord. of 6-25-85, § 2)

